Expected elements: present

Dense, legible, unmistakably the tool. The width split across the three columns is still wrong, and the new fade makes that visible rather than fixing it.

(a) The fade half-works. On the Transaction pane's RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE) block the ramp runs y1051-1074: 24px, exactly one 23px line-height. `"aztec": {` goes full-black at cap-height to ~50% at its baseline; the line above is untouched. The mid-glyph cut is gone, but one dim line reads as "the last line is grey", not as a progression. The same system already fades horizontally across ~3.7 characters (Code line 40, x880-905). Two to three line-heights would match it.

(b) Em dashes on SELECTOR/RAW correct; EXECUTIONS is a proper sentence. Cost values are not humanised: `88000 / 200000` sits beside the Call Trace's `1,315`, and the identity bar prints `1315` for the number the Call Trace prints `1,315`.

Re-measured, every figure holds. Call Trace region y68-669 (601px), content ends y328: 341px empty, 56.7% of the region, 59.4% below the tab strip. Values y674-1075, last rule y952: 123px, 30.7%. Widest frame row still leaves 153px dead (x1353-1506). Middle column 598px, Transaction 373px.

New argument: what overflows is prose, not data. DATA 6 lines + EXECUTIONS 3 + RAW 5 is ~320px, a third of the pane body, at 40-49 characters in a 373px column. +130px takes that to ~10 lines and recovers roughly the height the fade is apologising for.

Fixes: widen the Transaction pane 120-130px; lengthen the fade to ~50px.

Rating: 7/10

